  "kind": "event",
  "title": "Batu's Mongol western campaign",
  "summary": "A Mongol army under Batu Khan advanced west from 1237. It took Ryazan in December 1237, Vladimir in February 1238 and Kyiv at the end of 1240, then crushed the Hungarian army at Mohi in April 1241 and took Esztergom. The Mongols withdrew in spring 1242 after the death of Great Khan Ögedei, though the reason is debated.",
